# Acorn UI design

Follow [`design/README.md`](../../design/README.md) and [`design/tokens.md`](../../design/tokens.md). The sidebar imports `sid-ui/styles/joined.css` and wraps in `JoinedProvider`. Use design-system components first; Acorn CSS (`extension/src/sidebar/styles/`) only arranges them and styles Acorn-only pieces (Acorn Face, row logo mark, generate progress, plan steps).

## Shell

Header (live Acorn Face, "Acorn", active-tab line, worker `Badge` while busy, account `MoreMenu` with an `Avatar` whose dot is the connection), then a `PillNav` for Jobs / Ask / Tabs (hash links), then the panel. Settings and the Face guide open from the avatar menu as `Drawer`s. There is no footer strip and no sticky action bar.

## Now card and rows

Actions on the active tab live in `NowCard`: Fill page (primary), Generate and Recommend under it, or Remember this tab on an unremembered Custom tab. List rows share `SidebarListCard`: the whole row opens or focuses the tab, Preview is the one visible action, and everything else goes in the ⋯ `MoreMenu`. Rows are grouped "Ready to fill" / "Needs a résumé".

```tsx
// ❌ BAD: hand-built controls and raw values
<button className="my-pill" style={{ background: "#1f6feb" }}>Fill</button>

// ✅ GOOD
<Button variant="primary" icon={<Glyph name="edit" />} label="Fill page" onClick={onFill} />
```

## Notices

Expected failures (sign-in, socket, Fill, download) go through `pushAcornNotice` / `broadcastOperatorNotice`, which show design-system toasts. Do not `throw` or `console.error` them; Chrome's extension Errors list shows those.

```tsx
pushAcornNotice({
  kind: "error",
  title: "Couldn’t sign in",
  detail: "Sign in to Joined in this browser first.",
});
```

## Tokens

Joined tokens only (`--color-*`, `--spacing-*`, `--radius-*`, `--font-*`). No hex values, no px font sizes, no new `--acorn-*` colors. Acorn-only sizes are named custom properties next to their rule.
